This project includes kernel designs and inference features adapted from the
following open-source projects:

1. satellitedown/inkling-2-mini-abliterated-ingine (Apache License 2.0)
   https://github.com/satellitedown/inkling-2-mini-abliterated-ingine
   - Runtime-gated Fisher-LDA directional ablation tensor schema & projection formula
     (optional `--ablation <path.safetensors>` support in src/weights.zig,
     cuda/kernels_inkling.cu, and cuda/kernels_prefill.cu).
   - Blackwell Programmatic Dependent Launch (PDL) overlap pattern, 16-CTA cluster
     DSMEM/`mbarrier` BF16 controller & router kernels and 1-launch cluster decode
     attention (`mapa.shared::cluster`, `st.async.weak.shared::cluster`), spill-free
     16-column `U=3` FP8/NVFP4 `mma.m16n8k16` GEMVs & LM-head, and 128-CTA
     multi-block stochastic LM-head sampling with 64-bit Gumbel precision
     (cuda/kernels_common.cuh, cuda/kernels_gemv.cu, cuda/kernels_inkling.cu).
   - Device-side adaptive `{2, 4, 8}` DSpark speculative verify width selection via
     CUDA Graph conditional switch (`cudaGraphCondTypeSwitch`), Top-K `1024`
     multi-CTA radix Markov candidate selection, dynamic context shortlist
     extension, and Markov-head online softmax confidence scoring
     (cuda/kernels_dspark.cu, cuda/cuda_abi.cu, src/weights.zig, src/engine.zig).
   - Multi-stage `cp.async` `128x128x64` grouped MoE GEMM pipeline structure for
     prefill, specialized for Blackwell `cvt.rn.f16x2.e2m1x2` + FP16 MMA
     (cuda/kernels_prefill.cu).
   - Offline Fisher-LDA abliteration generation and refusal evaluation tools
     (tools/ablate.py, tools/inkling_ref.py, tools/refusal_eval.py,
     tools/pyproject.toml), adapted to run via `uv` and evaluate refusals via
     `squid5090 serve`.

2. AtomicBot-ai/atomic-engine (MIT License, llama.cpp fork)
   https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-engine/tree/codex/expert-weight-source
   - Inspiration for hybrid prompt-lookup speculative drafting with DSpark
     fallback (implemented from scratch as a zero-malloc O(1) hash-indexed
     PromptLookupIndex in src/engine.zig).

3. sybil-solutions/inference-optimisation-skill
   https://github.com/sybil-solutions/inference-optimisation-skill
   - Hardware-ceiling roofline methodology, noise-controlled hill-climbing
     workflow, and lever prioritization documented in LEARNINGS.md.

4. Inkling-2-Mini model architecture & tokenizer specification (Apache License 2.0)
   Thinking Machines / Inkling-2-Mini.
